fix: strip redundant base64 image data from tool response before storage

When MCP tools return images, the base64 data was stored in both the
ToolBlock (rawMcpToolResponse.response) and the ImageBlock
(generateImageResponse). Over multiple tool calls this caused JS heap
to balloon — measured at 924 MB of strings (84% of heap) in a session
with ~125 generated images.

Extract images before emitting MCP_TOOL_COMPLETE and replace the heavy
base64 payload in the tool response with a lightweight placeholder.
The ImageBlock continues to hold the actual image data for display.
The ToolBlock UI (extractPreviewContent) only reads content.mimeType,
never content.data, so display is unaffected.
